{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-039", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-039: Series-level AVOID share vs winning (talent confound)", "score": 1.189, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-CHT-039 (0.72)", "request matches RQC:RQC-103 (0.75); FAM:SF-CHT-039 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-103"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Series-level AVOID share vs winning (talent confound)", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Higher AVOID share predicts losing, independent of team quality.", "observed_result": "Game-level rho=-0.19 p=0.008 (inflated n, team-quality confound). Series-level rho=-0.26 p=0.07 (n=50, underpowered; ~80 series needed for p<0.05). Low AVOID-share bin 52.6% vs 25-50% bin 37.0%.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Series n=50 p=0.07; still confounded by team quality (OKC disciplined and good).", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=50 series; stated need ~80 for p<0.05", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "inconclusive"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:confounding"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:CONFOUNDING"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF01", "label": "Study family SF01: Suppression is not regression to mean: matched-control excess", "score": 0.726, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF01 (0.73)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Suppression is not regression to mean: matched-control excess", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "The H1-to-H2 PPP drop after a trigger exceeds the drop of a matched control, beyond what RTM predicts.", "observed_result": "PO C: excess +0.680 [0.619, 0.740], n=534, t=22.11; RTM pred 0.097 of 0.626 drop (15.5%), excess 0.529. Full graph unconstrained +0.628 n=9,900 then Z1+Z2 +0.625 n=9,111. H1-balanced caliper 0.10 +0.408 [0.378, 0.438], 1 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Excess drops from +0.625 unconstrained to +0.408 when balanced on H1 PPP, but the cluster CI excludes 0; Z1+Z2 moved excess only +0.004 vs pre-fix +0.404.", "observed_verdict": "supported", "auto_confidence": "high (1.0)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-050", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-050: Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star", "score": 0.712, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPM-022 auto_related_family (repeated_by_later_family) FAM:SF-APPA-050", "FAM:SF-APPM-022 auto_related_family (repeat_of_earlier_family) FAM:SF-APPA-050"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar sequential suppression: opponent play before the star", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "A specific opponent play type on the preceding possession suppresses each star's next-possession PPP relative to that star's baseline.", "observed_result": "PUTBACK is top suppressor for 6+ stars (e.g. D. Mitchell 1.178 to 0.884, d=-0.294, n_after=95; B. Beal d=-0.345 n=32; C. Holmgren d=-0.222 n=52). Other tops: TRANSITION (A. Davis -0.058), POST_UP (N. Jokic -0.075), PULL_ [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No multiplicity correction; n_after is 32-95 for several PUTBACK cells vs thousands of baseline possessions.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars; min n_after=30", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:DRIFT_NONSTATIONARITY"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-022", "label": "Study family SF-APPM-022: Superstar suppression profiles (incl. Q5c sequential triggering)", "score": 0.712, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPM-022 (0.71)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar suppression profiles (incl. Q5c sequential triggering)", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Specific opposing lineups, defenders, play types and preceding opponent play types suppress star efficiency.", "observed_result": "Q5c verdict 'rank-1 suppressor varies meaningfully across players'; e.g. Jokic after opp POST_UP 1.1271 (-0.0675, SE +/-0.0500, n=480); Curry forced POST_UP -0.209.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Rank-1 deltas mostly within 1-2 SE with no multiple-comparison control; OTHER artifact flagged in doc.", "observed_sample_and_power": "SE per cell reported", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "inconclusive", "observed_failure_type": "E_unclear", "observed_notes": "NOT_RECORDED", "auto_confidence": "medium (0.65)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-050"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-015", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-015: A3 equilibrium vs actual significance test", "score": 0.71, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPA-015 (0.71)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "A3 equilibrium vs actual significance test", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "Matchup-aware equilibrium beats actual team behavior significantly across matchups.", "observed_result": "A3 beats actual 138/240 (57.5%); weighted mean +2.06 pts/100; median +2.22; SD 14.26; t=2.24; p=0.0644.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Doc reports p=0.064 not significant.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=240, SD 14.26 pts/100", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Per-matchup A3 minus actual across 240 matchups; t-test.", "observed_verdict": "null", "observed_failure_type": "E_unclear", "observed_notes": "t=2.24 with n=240 should give p about 0.026 two-sided, so the stated p and t disagree. A3 PPP is nearly constant per offense, e.g. OKC 1.356 against every opponent."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPA-011"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-012", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-012: Defensive PPP allowed and possession share, RS vs playoffs", "score": 0.456, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-079 (0.72); FAM:SF-APPS-012 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-079"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Defensive PPP allowed and possession share, RS vs playoffs", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Playoff defenses suppress DRIVE more than RS defenses (both lower PPP allowed and lower share).", "observed_result": "DRIVE allowed 1.191 -> 0.923 (-0.268), share 21.2% -> 18.2%; PNR -0.139, share +12.1pp; PULL_UP +0.341, share -7.6pp.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No inferential test; PNR share jump of +12.1pp may reflect tagging differences.", "observed_sample_and_power": "25 teams", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "25 defensive teams, min 30 poss per cell; RS vs playoff PPP allowed and opponent possession share by PT.", "observed_verdict": "descriptive", "observed_failure_type": "E_unclear"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-058: Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "score": 0.455, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-051 (0.72); FAM:SF-APPA-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-051"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Each star's top sequential suppressor is stable across seasons, and some teammate X->Y sequences have large negative premiums.", "observed_result": "2/30 (7%) stable (>=75% same top suppressor): D. Mitchell PUTBACK 75%, L. James POST_UP 75%. Negative: J. Tatum->K. Porzingis DRIVE->SPOT_UP -0.444 n=31; Giannis->Lillard DRIVE->PNR -0.263 n=31; J. Brown->J. Tatum SPOT_U [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Only 2/30 stars meet the 75% same-top-suppressor stability rule.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars x 4 seasons; min n=20/cell", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF02", "label": "Study family SF02: Cost of ignoring suppression: continue rate and points lost", "score": 0.363, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF01 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF02"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Cost of ignoring suppression: continue rate and points lost", "auto_outcome_status": "inconclusive", "observed_hypothesis": "After a suppression trigger, teams keep running the suppressed play at near-H1 volume and lose several points per event.", "observed_result": ["[APPA-040] PO: 735 events; Group A 683 (93%) H1 1.522 to H2 0.876, cost/poss 0.646, ~8.2 H2 poss, ~97% H1 volume, ~5.4 pts/trigger; real actionable ~6.1 pts (5.3 keep-calling + 0.8 AVOID vs BEST). RS continue 93.1% (2,94 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "[APPS-021] Group A: H1 1.522 -> post-trigger 0.876, cost 0.646 PPP/poss, 5.16 pts/trigger (t=48.172, p=0.0000, n=683). Pivot vs continue overall H2 1.074 vs 1.043, MW p=0.2642. Locked row-mean (n>=5): H1 1.48->H2 0.85, d [cut; read_family for the full text]", "[CHT-040] H1-H2 drop t=48.172 p=0.0000 (n=683). Pivoting improve H2? Mann-Whitney p=0.2642 (not significant)."]}, "relationships": []}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-070", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-070: H1 usage as predictor of H2 suppression (distribution shift)", "score": 0.361, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-029 (0.72); FAM:SF-APPS-070 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-029"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "H1 usage as predictor of H2 suppression (distribution shift)", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "First-half reliance on a play type predicts second-half suppression after controlling for H1 PPP / mean reversion.", "observed_result": "Test B: all BH-adjusted null/WEAK (PNR ATT=+0.0313 BH_p=0.0658 WEAK; others NULL). Test C top-1 acc=0.550 vs mean-reversion baseline 0.511 (+0.039) vs most-used 0.239. Test A PULL_UP slope -0.0581 p=0.0030; CUT -0.0917 p [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Matched ATT does not survive BH; predictive lift over mean reversion is only +0.039 (0.550 vs 0.511). Bulk of H2 suppression is RTM.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=8873 team-games; Test C test n=1008"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:RTM_SELECTION"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-076", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-076: Trigger attribution: variance of H1->H2 PPP collapse", "score": 0.361, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-029 (0.72); FAM:SF-APPS-076 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-029"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Trigger attribution: variance of H1->H2 PPP collapse", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Observable in-game process/usage/shot-selection/lineup/context changes explain suppression triggers beyond RTM.", "observed_result": "RTM (ppp_h1 alone) 32.9% of variance. Usage +0.0%; process+shot-zone +1.7%; lineup +0.0%; context +0.0%. Unexplained 65.4%. Total explained 34.6% (RTM=95% of explained).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Process/usage/lineup/context add ~1.7 pp; residual 65.4% is idiosyncratic noise from small per-half n.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=40963 cells; 12617 triggers", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null", "observed_failure_type": "B_powered_null", "auto_confidence": "high (0.95)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPS-070"}, {"rel": "auto_addresses_question", "node": "RQC:RQC-029"}]}], "n_results": 10}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).
